      "about": "Alton Baker Pond and Canoe Canal are located within Alton Baker Park, one of the most popular and multi-functional parks in Eugene.\nThe park is located on the north bank of the Willamette River just east of the Ferry Street Bridge and Coburg Road. It is accessible by foot or bike from either side of the river via the River Bank Trails. By car you can enter via the Club Road underpass off Coburg Road or from Autzen Stadium off MLK/Centennial.\nLocated with in the park are two ponds and a canal, which can be accessed by rented canoes during the summer months.\nTROUT STOCKING SCHEDULE -- https://myodfw.com/fishing/species/trout/stocking-schedul
